     "In 1943, a seventeen year old Swede named Ingvar Kamprad started a business selling pens, wallets and picture frames by mail."
    ],
    [
     "b02_2",
     {
      "bg": "home",
      "cast": [],
      "props": [
       {
        "type": "note",
        "x": 960,
        "y": 560,
        "s": 1.4,
        "lines": [
         "I.K. = Ingvar Kamprad",
         "E = Elmtaryd farm",
         "A = Agunnaryd village"
        ]
       }
      ]
     },
     "He called it IKEA. His initials, plus the farm and village where he grew up."
    ],
    [
     "b02_3",
     {
      "bg": "office",
      "cast": [
       {
